  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which neomycin may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 (UGT2B4), a key enzyme involved in drug metabolism and detoxification. Neomycin is linked to multiple targets, including Multidrug Resistance-Associated Protein 7 (MRP7) and Induced Myeloid Leukemia Cell Differentiation Protein Mcl-1, which are both targets of other compounds. These targets are ultimately engaged by UGT2B4, indicating a possible pathway where neomycin may indirectly influence UGT2B4 activity through these intermediate molecules. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, with neomycin acting as a modulator of UGT2B4 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on UGT2B4 underscores the complexity of the system, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of neomycin in UGT2B4 inhibition or regulation.",
